                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">By the President of the United States of
                        America.</hi></head>
                <dateline>[<placeName>The Hague</placeName>, <date
                        ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1904-12-21">December 21, 1904</date>]</dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">A PROCLAMATION.</p>
                <p>Whereas a Convention providing for the exemption of Hospital Ships in time of war
                    from the payment of all dues and taxes imposed for the benefit of the State was
                    signed at The Hague on December 21, 1904, by the Plenipotentiaries of the United
                    States of America, Germany, Austria-Hungary, Belgium, China, Korea, Denmark,
                    Spain, Mexico, France, Greece, Italy, Japan, Luxemburg, Montenegro, The
                    Netherlands, Peru, Persia, Portugal, Roumania, Russia, Servia, Siam, and
                    Switzerland, the original of which Convention in the French language is word for
                    word as follows:</p>




